{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Priya. I'd like to start with membership. I recommend the council include equal representation from both legacy groups -- say, two members from each -- to ensure balanced perspectives. On format, monthly meetings for the first several sessions sounds right, and I'd suggest a rotating facilitation model rather than a single fixed chair, so no one person bears the full burden and it builds shared ownership. For safeguards, I think a clear confidentiality protocol, a public agenda set in advance, and the written summary to you after each meeting are all essential. I do want to flag one thing transparently: I had an informal discussion with the outgoing transition chair about potentially chairing this council for an initial period, but that was never documented or formally agreed. I want to make sure any role I might play is something you explicitly approve as part of this process, not something carried over from a side conversation."}
```

